# Every path is owned, so a pull request always requests a review from someone.
#
# CODEOWNERS only has teeth behind a branch protection rule or ruleset with
# "Require review from Code Owners" turned on; on its own it is a request, not a
# gate.
#
# A handle here that has no write access to the repository is silently ignored by
# GitHub (no error, no review request), so check access before adding one.
# @seandean approves every change: the account that writes a pull request (usually
# @distronode-com) can never approve it, so the owner must be a different person.
